<title>JAPAN: Israel to launch samurai bond by June - sources.</title>
<headline>Israel to launch samurai bond by June - sources.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Israel is expected to launch its first yen-denominated bonds in Japan by June, market sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The lead manager is expected to be chosen in March and the bond is likely to be launched during the April-June quarter, they said.</p>
<p>The samurai is likely to be a medium-term bond with less than 10 years to maturity, the sources said.</p>
<p>The issue amount is likely to be up to 20 billion yen, although details have yet to be decided, they said.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-9780</p>
</text>
